# browser-plugin.xcl - drive a browser through the `xcelerate.browser` plugin.
#
# The plugin owns the browser API: every op forwards to the host's semantic
# browser bridge (`host.browser`), never raw CDP/BiDi. It needs the `browser`
# capability granted, and the XCL `run` verb allowlisted:
#
#   XCELERATE_PLUGIN_ALLOW=browser \
#     xcelerate --browser brave --plugins browser \
#               run --allow-plugin xcelerate.browser browser-plugin.xcl
#
# `--plugins browser` resolves ./plugins/browser, then ~/.xcl/plugins/browser,
# then a path you pass. `--browser brave` picks the Chromium browser to drive.

run xcelerate.browser open {"url":"https://example.com"}
run xcelerate.browser title
run xcelerate.browser text

# The core verbs still work alongside the plugin (the page is bound to it):
assert url contains example.com

done
